From beca4b8a30ddd1ffa5bc0f35578366a7c4b1b449 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 01:03:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/19] Widen the AFAC margins from 17 to 22 months

The carrier side came from a file already on disk: DATATUR republishes AFAC's
airline series as one long table running to July 2026, and it reproduces the
seventeen months already in the repository to the passenger, so it is the same
source without the anti-automation challenge that blocks gob.mx downloads.
The route side gained 2026M01 to 2026M07 from the July 2026 cumulative
workbook, retrieved through the Internet Archive.

Twenty of the twenty-two months now reconcile exactly between the two
independently published margins, up from fifteen of seventeen -- the evidence
that a joint table exists upstream is that much stronger.

Replace the throwaway script that built these with a module that states the
workbook layout it depends on, drops the year-to-date months that carry no
passengers rather than emitting empty routes, and returns the reconciliation
instead of printing it.

2025M04 to 2025M12 stays open on the route side: gob.mx answers every .xlsx
URL with the same 1,936-byte challenge page, valid or invented, so the file
path cannot even be confirmed by probing, and Save Page Now now requires an
account. The doc records how to close it from an ordinary browser in a minute.

